## [2026-03-22 00:02:00 UTC] Phase 1 — Critical Fixes (Security, Correctness, Packaging)

### Context
- Production-grade improvement plan approved by user
- Phase 1 addresses: sys.path hack, URL injection, dependency declarations, empty __init__.py, bare excepts, dead imports
- Files to modify: api.py, strings_and_lists.py, __init__.py (x2), pyproject.toml, test_api.py

### Action Taken
- Removed sys.path hack (lines 3-7) from api.py, converted `from utils.*` to relative imports (`from .utils.*`)
- Removed dead `import pandas as pd` from api.py
- Fixed URL injection in 5 methods: moved user input from f-string URLs to `params` dict
- Fixed 3 bare except clauses in api.py and strings_and_lists.py
- Populated both `__init__.py` files with proper exports
- Updated pyproject.toml: removed pandas, added numpy (temporary until Phase 2)
- Updated test_api.py: changed URL-string assertions to verify params dict

### Outcome
- Success — 95 tests passing in 0.08s
- `from data_gov_uk import DataGovUk` now works
- No more URL injection vulnerability or bare except clauses

### Bugs / Errors Encountered
N/A

### Fix or Mitigation
N/A

### Pitfalls & Future Risks
- The `include_datasets` param is now passed as string "True"/"False" — CKAN API accepts this but worth verifying

### Best Practices & Lessons Learned
- Always use `params` dict for query parameters instead of f-string interpolation to prevent injection

